  "released": "2007-08-21",
  "notes": "Main artist written as \"MIA\" on front cover, \"M.I.A\" on the spine, and \"M.I.A.\" on hype sticker.\n\nStandard jewel case with clear tray, 16 page booklet and double-sided inlay.\n\nText on hype sticker: 'M.I.A. KALA \"A triumph for its revolutionary creator\" NME \"M.I.A. at her most masterful\" The Observer Album of the Week \"Defiantly brilliant\" Daily Telegraph \"Glorious\" The Sun INCLUDES THE HIT SINGLE PAPER PLANES'\n\nTrack 1 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control. Incorporates elements of \"Roadrunner\", written by Jonathan Richman, published by Modern Love Songs/Rockin' Leprechaun Music; \"Kaattukkuyilu\" from the film \"Dalapathi\", written and performed by Ilaiyaraja, licensed courtesy of GV Films Ltd.\nTrack 2 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control. Incorporates elements of \"Thirvizha Na Vantha\" from the film \"Jayam\" written and performed by R.P. Patnaik, licensed courtesy of Jeyam Company.\nTrack 3 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control.\nTrack 4 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control. Incorporates elements of \"Jimmy Jimmy Aaja Aaja\" from the film \"Disco Dancer\", written by Bappi Lahiri, published by Saregama.\nTrack 5 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control/Hollertronix Music (ASCAP).\nTrack 6 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control. Remixed from the original recording \"Down River\" by the Wilcannia Mob, created in the town of Wilcannia, NSW for a community project by Shopfront Theatre for Young People, Sydney, Australia. \nTrack 7 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control. Incorporates elements of \"Where Is My Mind\", written by Charles Thompson, published by Songs Of Universal / Rice and Beans Music.\nTrack 8 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Copyright Control. Incorporates elements of \"Hands Up, Thumbs Down\" written by Blaqstarr, published by JB Starr Publishing.\nTrack 9 published by Zomba Music Publishing/JB Starr Productions.\nTrack 10 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Hollertronix Music (ASCAP)/Copyright Control.\nTrack 11 published by Zomba Music Publishing/Hollertronix Music (ASCAP). Incorporates elements of \"Straight To Hell\", written by Joe Strummer, Mick Jones, Paul Simonon and Topper Headon, published by Nineden Ltd./Universal Music Publishing Ltd./Universal Polygram International.\nTrack 12 published by Virginia Beach Music Publishing/Warner Chappell Publishing (ASCAP)/Stix I'm Stoned Publishing/Universal Music Publishing (ASCAP)/Zomba Music Publishing. Mixed at Chalice Studios Los Angeles, CA.\n\n℗&© 2007 XL Recordings Ltd.",
